    "summary": "- `GET /api/invoices` accepts `limit` (default 20, integer 1–100) and `cursor`, returning `{\"items\", \"next_cursor\"}` in (created, id) order. Invalid `limit` gives 400 `invalid_limit`; an unreadable cursor gives 400 `invalid_cursor`.\n- Paging is stable under concurrent inserts: walking all pages returns each invoice exactly once, with no skips or repeats.\n- New Go tests cover the page walk, the last-page and empty cases, limit validation, cursor validation, and an insert between page requests. `go build ./...`, `go test ./...` and `go vet ./...` pass.",
